1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,627
Nearly half of Americans earning over

2
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:05,113
one hundred thousand dollars a year

3
00:00:05,113 --> 00:00:06,959
live paycheck to paycheck.

4
00:00:06,959 --> 00:00:09,160
A story from 1769 explains why.

5
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:09,819
In 1769,

6
00:00:09,819 --> 00:00:13,197
the philosopher Denis Diderot wrote about

7
00:00:13,197 --> 00:00:15,751
a luxurious scarlet robe he had

8
00:00:15,751 --> 00:00:16,657
been given.

9
00:00:16,657 --> 00:00:18,140
Next to that robe,

10
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,282
his old desk looked cheap.

11
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:22,259
So he replaced the desk.

12
00:00:22,259 --> 00:00:23,742
Then the tapestry.

13
00:00:23,742 --> 00:00:25,060
Then the chairs.

14
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:28,320
The anthropologist Grant McCracken later named

15
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,021
this the Diderot Effect.

16
00:00:30,021 --> 00:00:32,289
You rarely buy just one upgrade.

17
00:00:32,289 --> 00:00:34,202
You buy a new identity that

18
00:00:34,202 --> 00:00:36,470
demands more purchases to match.

19
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:37,796
To break the spiral,

20
00:00:37,796 --> 00:00:39,719
use the Invisible Raise Rule:

21
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:41,509
whenever your income jumps,

22
00:00:41,509 --> 00:00:44,492
automatically route fifty percent into assets

23
00:00:44,492 --> 00:00:46,680
before it ever hits your checking

24
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:47,210
account.

25
00:00:47,210 --> 00:00:49,691
Real wealth isn't what people see

26
00:00:49,691 --> 00:00:50,968
in your driveway,

27
00:00:50,968 --> 00:00:53,900
it's the freedom you didn't trade away.
